WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.073
<v Examiner>Exam case 9, continued.

2
00:00:03.073 --> 00:00:05.677
<v Examiner>Label the synapse, and why levodopa.

3
00:00:06.127 --> 00:00:10.301
In her session she said you will get this specific drawing in the exam.

4
00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:15.592
And in another: they're going to ask you to pinpoint the presynaptic neuron, and label it.

5
00:00:15.592 --> 00:00:18.649
So these are free marks, if the letters are learned.

6
00:00:19.099 --> 00:00:19.827
<v Examiner>Nine marks.

7
00:00:19.827 --> 00:00:25.115
<v Examiner>Label her synapse figure, A to G, and name the two transport processes it shows.

8
00:00:25.565 --> 00:00:27.332
The hook: vesicles mean pre.

9
00:00:27.332 --> 00:00:28.595
Receptors mean post.

10
00:00:29.045 --> 00:00:32.693
Letter A is a calcium channel, where calcium enters the cell.

11
00:00:33.143 --> 00:00:36.385
B is a vesicle, which contains the neurotransmitters.

12
00:00:36.835 --> 00:00:39.284
C is the neurotransmitter molecules.

13
00:00:39.284 --> 00:00:40.441
Every dot is one.

14
00:00:40.891 --> 00:00:45.605
D is a reuptake channel, where the neurotransmitter goes back, to be used again.

15
00:00:46.055 --> 00:00:49.213
E is the receptors, on the postsynaptic membrane.

16
00:00:49.663 --> 00:00:51.518
F is the presynaptic neuron.

17
00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:53.439
You can tell by the vesicles.

18
00:00:53.889 --> 00:00:55.881
G is the postsynaptic neuron.

19
00:00:55.881 --> 00:00:57.942
You can tell by the receptors.

20
00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:00.938
Then the two processes.

21
00:01:00.938 --> 00:01:06.517
Exocytosis: the vesicle fuses with the membrane, and releases the neurotransmitter.

22
00:01:06.517 --> 00:01:10.684
And diffusion: the neurotransmitters cross the synaptic cleft,

23
00:01:10.684 --> 00:01:12.768
from high concentration to low.

24
00:01:13.218 --> 00:01:16.999
Her formative test words the same figure as drop-downs.

25
00:01:16.999 --> 00:01:23.049
B is a vesicle containing neurotransmitters, such as serotonin, epinephrine or dopamine.

26
00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:26.143
E is a receptor on the postsynaptic membrane.

27
00:01:26.143 --> 00:01:30.680
The process moving neurotransmitters into the cleft is exocytosis.

28
00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:35.149
And the process moving them across the cleft is simple diffusion.

29
00:01:36.599 --> 00:01:37.393
<v Examiner>Three marks.

30
00:01:37.393 --> 00:01:42.754
<v Examiner>Levodopa travels through the blood and into the brain, and is used as medication.

31
00:01:42.754 --> 00:01:44.343
<v Examiner>Why not dopamine itself?

32
00:01:44.793 --> 00:01:49.728
To work on brain cells, a medication must be able to cross the blood-brain barrier.

33
00:01:49.728 --> 00:01:53.652
Substances that aren't lipid soluble, fat soluble, can't cross it,

34
00:01:53.652 --> 00:01:56.981
so they're useless for treating conditions of the brain.

35
00:01:56.981 --> 00:02:00.608
And the third line, which is the textbook's rather than hers:

36
00:02:00.608 --> 00:02:04.473
levodopa crosses into the brain, and is made into dopamine there.

37
00:02:04.473 --> 00:02:07.683
Dopamine itself doesn't cross the blood-brain barrier.

38
00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:10.765
Her Kahoot makes the same point with alcohol:

39
00:02:10.765 --> 00:02:14.917
alcohol affects the brain because it can cross the blood-brain barrier.

40
00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:16.002
<v Examiner>Once more.

41
00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:18.098
<v Examiner>The synapse labels, and levodopa.

42
00:02:20.548 --> 00:02:22.356
Letter A, a calcium channel.

43
00:02:22.356 --> 00:02:24.486
B, a vesicle of neurotransmitter.

44
00:02:24.486 --> 00:02:26.681
C, the neurotransmitter molecules.

45
00:02:26.681 --> 00:02:28.102
D, a reuptake channel.

46
00:02:28.102 --> 00:02:29.199
E, the receptors.

47
00:02:29.199 --> 00:02:32.105
F, the presynaptic neuron, with the vesicles.

48
00:02:32.105 --> 00:02:35.139
G, the postsynaptic neuron, with the receptors.

49
00:02:35.139 --> 00:02:38.819
Into the cleft by exocytosis, and across it by diffusion.

50
00:02:38.819 --> 00:02:44.501
Levodopa, not dopamine, because a drug must cross the blood-brain barrier to work on the

51
00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:44.888
brain.

52
00:02:44.888 --> 00:02:49.924
Levodopa crosses and is made into dopamine there; dopamine itself can't cross.
